    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33155" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostentārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		ostentum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to prophetic
				indications</i>, <i>prophetic</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostentaria novitas (al. ostentatoria),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2, § 151</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostentārĭum</span></b> , ii,
				n., <i>a book of prognostics</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tuscum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 3, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arborarium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
